    description: "FOUND 2026-10-13 by WI-tusad F4 (INV-punig two-parent probes); coverage gap, not identity.\n\nREPRO: rtl/a.v\n  module a;\n    task run; begin end endtask\n    function integer f; input x; f = x; endfunction\n    wire w;\n  endmodule\n`hypergumbo run --include-docs` emits only `module a`: tasks, functions (and nets) inside a module produce no symbol, so calls into them have no target and the module's internals are invisible. The F3 live check listed verilog as \"clean\" on a nested-task probe for this reason: nothing was emitted to move.\n\nThe stable_id gate lists verilog in FLAT_LANGUAGES (\"only modules and interfaces are emitted\"); emitting tasks/functions will make it nest, and the gate will then demand a two-parent fixture (module a / module b each with `task run`)."  # 2ddb
    fields: {}  # 2ddb
